<script>
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import notes from '#lib/data/desk-notes.json';
  import { groupByCause, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';
  import Callout from '#lib/kb/Callout.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';

  const ISSUES = 'https://github.com/kamyk-pl/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/';
  const merged = uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === 4471);
  const oneDay = merged.filter((r) => notes.oneDayMove.includes(r.id));
  const byCause = groupByCause(merged.filter((r) => !notes.oneDayMove.includes(r.id)), tenantOf);
  const count = (cause) => byCause.find((g) => g.cause === cause)?.reports.length ?? 0;
  const split = [
    { problem: 'parser', what: 'day and month swapped by the shared parser', n: count('parser'), issue: 1 },
    { problem: 'hint', what: 'booking-v3 form hints MM/DD to day-first tenants', n: count('hint'), issue: 2 },
    { problem: 'one-day', what: 'date moves by one day', n: oneDay.length, issue: 4 },
  ];
</script>

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own table already disagrees: it
shows a second cause with no ticket of its own and a footnote about one-day moves. Read by cause
instead of by subject, the reports hold three problems. Each one has its own ticket now, and
fixing one does not close the others.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 will not stop the booking-v3 form reports or the one-day moves.
Keep #4471 open until all three tickets are closed.
</Callout>

## The split

**{merged.length}** reports in #4471, each in one ticket:

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>problem</th><th>reports</th><th>ticket</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    {#each split as row}
      <tr>
        <td><code>{row.problem}</code> · {row.what}</td>
        <td>{row.n}</td>
        <td><a href={ISSUES + row.issue}>issue {row.issue}</a></td>
      </tr>
    {/each}
  </tbody>
</table>

Counted with the desk's own code: one report per id (`uniqueById`), cause by tenant and form
(`causes.ts`), not by intake tag. The one-day moves are the reports the desk itself noted in
`desk-notes.json`. [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) files them under `parser`; here they are taken out
of `parser` and counted once, in their own ticket.

## `parser`: day and month swapped

Ticket: [https://github.com/kamyk-pl/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1](https://github.com/kamyk-pl/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)

**What people see.** A date with day and month swapped: booked 7 April, invite for 4 July. Every
date in these reports has a day of 12 or less, because a day above 12 cannot be read as a month.

**Who.** Every tenant on file writes the day first. The app and email channels on any tenant, and
the form on booking-v2 tenants, whose hint says DD/MM.

**Fix.** The shared parser has to read dates in the tenant's locale, not month first. This is the
fix #4471 already queued.

## `hint`: the booking-v3 form asks for the month first

Ticket: [https://github.com/kamyk-pl/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2](https://github.com/kamyk-pl/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)

**What people see.** The same swap, but only through the booking form of Alder Physio,
Copper Studio and Pale Harbour.

**Why it is different.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what
the hint tells them, month first, and the form reads it the tenant's way, day first. The parser
fix does not touch this path.

**Fix.** The hint under the field has to follow the tenant's locale, like booking-v2's
`DD/MM/YYYY` for day-first tenants.

## `one-day`: the date moves by one day

Ticket: [https://github.com/kamyk-pl/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/4](https://github.com/kamyk-pl/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/4)

**What people see.** Not a swap. Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May. A client in Lisbon gets
Tuesday and a client in Toronto gets Monday for the same meeting. An invite arrives before the
booking was made.

**Why it is different.** The desk had already read these as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`),
but #4471 files them under `parser` by tenant. They belong to this ticket, not the `parser` one. The date is converted across time zones, so it
lands on the neighbouring day. It needs a separate look at how invites store and send times.

**Fix.** Unknown yet. Start from these reports.

## Why one ticket hid three

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match.
  These subjects (wrong day, wrong date, dates mixed up) describe a symptom, not a cause, so
  three causes merged into one ticket.
- The intake tag is a guess from the browser, and it disagrees with the tenant in both directions.
- The export repeats some reports across pages. Counting raw rows inflates the queue.

Decision records are never edited after they are accepted, so 0001 needs a successor. Until then,
read the body before merging a report about dates.

